   ],
   "textLength": 247,
   "text": "You can have restaurant-style General Tso’s chicken ready in just 30 minutes at home.\nThe process skips marinating, so you save time without giving up bold flavor.\nThe sauce can be made up to three days in advance for even smoother weeknight prep.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 3,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 0,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1360,
    "height": 194,
    "widthFraction": 0.38,
    "leftFraction": 0.17,
    "pageFraction": 0.12,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 7,
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "mntl-sc-block_2-0",
   "class": "comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 360,
   "text": "At my house, the presentation of General Tso’s chicken at the dinner table is typically in a white paper takeout carton or Styrofoam clamshell. Those gooey little nuggets still manage to hit the spot even though I know they’ll be subpar: too soggy, too greasy, too sweet. The deep-fried nature of General Tso’s doesn’t hold up to travel well, even across town.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1627,
    "height": 135,
    "widthFraction": 0.42,
    "leftFraction": 0.15,
    "pageFraction": 0.15,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 8,
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "mntl-sc-block_4-0",
   "class": "comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 392,
   "text": "For a General Tso’s worth remembering, plan ahead and make it at home. It feels magical to conjure up a super-fresh upgrade of a Chinese takeout classic, and the results are transformative. The exterior is crispy and glistening with superbly balanced sauce. The chicken itself is juicy and piping hot. Pair it with steamed white rice to capture all that sauce and everyone will be spellbound.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.05,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1778,
    "height": 162,
    "widthFraction": 0.42,
    "leftFraction": 0.15,
    "pageFraction": 0.16,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
