  },
  {
   "index": 14,
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "mntl-sc-block_14-0",
   "class": "comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 241,
   "text": "You’ll often see cornstarch in frying recipes because cornstarch helps make fried foods crispy. Since cornstarch doesn’t brown well, in this recipe you’ll mix it with all-purpose flour to enable a golden-brown exterior. It’s a win-win combo.",
