   "textLength": 676,
   "text": "If you don’t have a thermometer, try this go-to trick for Chinese cooks. Stick a wooden chopstick in the hot oil. If you see a few bubbles that don’t move quickly, keep heating. Lots of bubbling around the chopstick means the oil is about 350°F, ready for you to start frying. \nFrying the chicken in batches keeps the pan from getting too crowded. Too much chicken in the oil at once makes its temper",
