   "textLength": 369,
   "text": "This dish is best eaten right after it’s made, but you can whisk the sauce together up to three days in advance and refrigerate it in an airtight container. Wait until right before cooking to add the cornstarch so it doesn’t thicken on the bottom of the sauce. You can also cut the chicken pieces up to two days in advance and refrigerate them in an airtight container.",
